=== eval.jsonl ===
{"id": "easy-00000457", "label": "-8048", "metadata": {"difficulty": "easy", "historical_accuracy": 0.875, "source_line": 457}, "prompt": [{"content": "Let $f(x)=x^{2}+a x+b$ and $g(x)=x^{2}+c x+d$ be two distinct real polynomials such that the $x$-coordinate of the vertex of $f$ is a root of $g$, the $x$-coordinate of the vertex of $g$ is a root of $f$ and both $f$ and $g$ have the same minimum value. If the graphs of the two polynomials intersect at the point (2012, - 2012), what is the value of $a+c$ ?\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.", "role": "user"}]}
{"id": "hard-00008633", "label": "(0, 4)", "metadata": {"difficulty": "hard", "historical_accuracy": 0.125, "source_line": 8633}, "prompt": [{"content": "Determine the interval of convergence for the series \\( \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\left(\\frac{n - i}{i - 2n}\\right)^{n} (z-2)^{n} \\).\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.", "role": "user"}]}
{"id": "easy-00021826", "label": "Yes", "metadata": {"difficulty": "easy", "historical_accuracy": 0.875, "source_line": 21826}, "prompt": [{"content": "Let $g$ be a function that is continuous on $(0, 1)$. If $\\int_{0+}^{1-} |g(x)|^q \\, dx$ converges for some $q > 1$, does it imply that $\\int_{0+}^{1-} |g(x)| \\, dx$ converges? Provide a justification for your answer.\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.", "role": "user"}]}
{"id": "hard-00008640", "label": "(0, 2]", "metadata": {"difficulty": "hard", "historical_accuracy": 0.0, "source_line": 8640}, "prompt": [{"content": "Determine the values of $k$ for which the Fourier cosine transform of $e^{-x^k}$, defined as \\[ g_k(z) = \\int_0^\\infty \\cos(zx) e^{-x^k} \\, dx, \\] is non-negative and decreasing for $z \\in \\mathbb{R}^{+}$. Provide your answer as a set of values for $k$.\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.", "role": "user"}]}
{"id": "easy-00006414", "label": "34", "metadata": {"difficulty": "easy", "historical_accuracy": 0.875, "source_line": 6414}, "prompt": [{"content": "A right rectangular prism has 6 faces, 12 edges, and 8 vertices. A new pyramid is to be constructed using one of the rectangular faces as the base. Calculate the maximum possible sum of the number of exterior faces, vertices, and edges of the combined solid (prism and pyramid).\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.", "role": "user"}]}
{"id": "hard-00028362", "label": "6", "metadata": {"difficulty": "hard", "historical_accuracy": 0.0, "source_line": 28362}, "prompt": [{"content": "长为正整数 $l$ 的木棒每次都可锯成长均为正整数的 2 段，可连续进行这种操作，但要求任何时刻所有木棒中的最长者长小于最短者长的 2 倍。例如，一根长为 6 的木棒只能截成长均为 3 的两段；一根长为 7 的木棒只能截成长分别为 $2,2,3$ 的三段。试问:长为 30 的木棒最多可锯成多少段?\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.", "role": "user"}]}
{"id": "easy-00004256", "label": "14", "metadata": {"difficulty": "easy", "historical_accuracy": 0.875, "source_line": 4256}, "prompt": [{"content": "In $\\triangle ABC$, $a$, $b$, $c$ are the sides opposite to $\\angle A$, $\\angle B$, $\\angle C$ respectively. If $\\cos 2B + \\cos B + \\cos (A-C) = 1$ and $b = \\sqrt{7}$, find the minimum value of $a^2 + c^2$.\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.", "role": "user"}]}
{"id": "hard-00001207", "label": "1540", "metadata": {"difficulty": "hard", "historical_accuracy": 0.125, "source_line": 1207}, "prompt": [{"content": "Determine the number of 8-tuples of nonnegative integers $\\left(a_{1}, a_{2}, a_{3}, a_{4}, b_{1}, b_{2}, b_{3}, b_{4}\\right)$ satisfying $0 \\leq a_{k} \\leq k$, for each $k=1,2,3,4$, and $a_{1}+a_{2}+a_{3}+a_{4}+2 b_{1}+3 b_{2}+4 b_{3}+5 b_{4}=19$.\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.", "role": "user"}]}
{"id": "easy-00007950", "label": "No", "metadata": {"difficulty": "easy", "historical_accuracy": 0.875, "source_line": 7950}, "prompt": [{"content": "If $f_n$ converges weakly to $f$ in $L^p(\\mathbb{R}^d)$ for $1<p<\\infty$, does $|f_n|$ converge weakly to $|f|$ in the same space?\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.", "role": "user"}]}
